{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787089248694514001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"sullen-famished-incatern","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3e9193c1793176550a5f34914b8f32798e8552c9030348c1fb4d14c18d4e2309","event_uuid":"e2ee7a2e-879d-4006-8c01-151273a8ae9e","position":{"commit_sha":"e2bae884796b7698e93ffd429c824a62f4a5d10d","position":"1787081121609742001-e2ee7a2e-879d-4006-8c01-151273a8ae9e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a899c0e816cd2e6a391cc18387026527e137915e22daf9a34fbd2b8e3cc28172","event_uuid":"39701f04-9c68-4582-95c3-ef51cd57a89b","position":{"commit_sha":"cb940551775f58f24c83f11fd8430ee2b3d189a7","position":"1787081141012747001-39701f04-9c68-4582-95c3-ef51cd57a89b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d9cd2e3d4f332b3e1707384bbbb8ee3c85fab9e953f18d1a34055d8d49bb7733","event_uuid":"9217834a-7059-4944-bb50-a41237a8c6ad","position":{"commit_sha":"150fedf1f9f7fcc5be7118443b2d4b1c5fd9d6c0","position":"1787081317212252001-9217834a-7059-4944-bb50-a41237a8c6ad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787081121609742001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9217834a-7059-4944-bb50-a41237a8c6ad","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"cfb7-f2ce-ce8a-4cfd"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAn indeterminate plan review can contain expensive successful calls plus a small retryable coverage gap. A normal rerun repeats everything, while blindly resuming old checkpoints risks applying results to changed material or policy. The maintainer approved an explicit `rebar review-plan --retry` override that resumes only the literal latest eligible review and authorizes a fresh attempt budget.\n\n## Approach\nAdd CLI parsing and a narrow library-internal retry request that reads the latest completed versioned RP-06 review journal. Eligibility requires that exact latest review to be `INDETERMINATE` with retryable missing calls. The lineage must be digest-complete and content-identical across ticket material, code/ref, effective policy, prompts/contracts, model/mode, topology, context, dependencies, and source. Legacy `REVIEW_RESULT` payloads and legacy checkpoints never seed retry.\n\nReuse every eligible successful unit, including clean and blocking results, and call only missing units. Budget-shed units remain missing. Pass-2 verification and coaching reuse unchanged per-finding successes and run only for newly recovered work; deterministic decision, assembly, signature eligibility, and narrow response rendering rerun over the combined result. Each explicit `--retry` grants a fresh per-invocation attempt budget. Cumulative lineage spend is stored as audit telemetry and never blocks a later explicit retry.\n\nFail before any model call when the latest result is not eligible or when its journal is missing, stale, corrupt, legacy, or digest-mismatched. Refusal is not a silent full review and gives the operator the normal full-review remedy. `--retry` is mutually exclusive with `--force`, `--status`, and `--check`; `--no-sign` remains compatible. Normal review behavior is unchanged without the flag.\n\nDocument the flag in the native canonical `review-plan --help`, generated `docs/cli-reference.md`, `docs/user-guide.md`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, and `docs/exit-codes.md`. Documentation must explain eligibility, fresh budget, reused blockers/successes, zero-call refusal, incompatible flags, signing behavior, and the distinction from `--status` and `sign-review`. Review and status responses remain narrow end-result views; the retry journal is not printed.\n\n## Migration and Rollback\nThe flag is additive and opt-in. Older journals are deliberately ineligible, so rollout needs no data rewrite. Removing the CLI flag and retry reader restores full-review-only behavior while leaving reducer-ignored journals harmless. Normal review remains the documented fallback for any refusal.\n\n## Testing\nUse a real CLI subprocess with a temporary ticket store plus the production journal codec and stateful fake at the model boundary. Assert exit code, stdout/stderr contract, exact called unit ids, stored lineage, and final verdict. Fault and negative-control cases assert zero calls. A generated-help test proves the documented flag is derived from canonical help rather than hand-maintained drift.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given a literal latest completed `INDETERMINATE` RP-06 journal with two successful units and one retryable missing unit, `rebar review-plan <id> --retry` calls only the missing unit and combines all three content-identical results.\n- [ ] Clean and blocking successes are reusable, budget-shed units remain missing, verification/coaching call only for newly recovered findings, and deterministic decision/assembly reruns over the combined set.\n- [ ] Each explicit retry receives the normal fresh per-invocation attempt budget; cumulative lineage usage is recorded but never enforced as a cap.\n- [ ] A latest `PASS`/`BLOCK`, a non-retryable indeterminate result, or a missing, legacy, corrupt, stale, or digest-mismatched journal refuses before any model/provider call and never falls through to a full review.\n- [ ] CLI contract tests prove `--retry` conflicts with `--force`, `--status`, and `--check`, remains compatible with `--no-sign`, and preserves normal no-flag behavior.\n- [ ] Retry output and `review-plan --status` expose only established end-result fields and no per-unit execution trace or verbose journal details.\n- [ ] Canonical `review-plan --help`, generated CLI reference, user guide, plan-review gate guide, and exit-code guide document eligibility, fresh budget, reuse/refusal behavior, flag interactions, signing, and the normal-full-review remedy.\n- [ ] A real CLI subprocess test proves the eligible resume path, zero-call refusal path, persisted retry lineage, and final exit/verdict semantics end to end.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py","reason":"Parse, validate, and render the explicit review-plan --retry operation."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/retry.py","reason":"Eligibility, digest validation, lineage reuse, and fresh-budget retry orchestration."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"Route the additive retry request through the normal review entry point and narrow result assembly."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py","reason":"Read and append versioned retry lineage without legacy seeding."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_retry.py","reason":"Eligibility, call reuse, fresh budget, flag, signing, refusal, and output contract tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_cli_retry.py","reason":"Real CLI subprocess and exit-code coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Canonical help and generated-reference drift guard."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Generated command reference including --retry."},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"Operator workflow and full-review fallback."},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Authoritative eligibility, lineage, signing, and refusal semantics."},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"Retry success, refusal, and transient exit behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","cfb7-f2ce-ce8a-4cfd"],["parent","58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp-06","llm","plan-review","cli","docs"],"ticket_id":"df80-d453-2267-4953","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-06 S5 — Add exact review-plan retry and canonical documentation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e2ee7a2e-879d-4006-8c01-151273a8ae9e","39701f04-9c68-4582-95c3-ef51cd57a89b","9217834a-7059-4944-bb50-a41237a8c6ad"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787089248694514001,"uuid":"40e1c71a-f162-4056-ab36-79241a9fa381"}